|name2 = 885-2
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''885-2''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
885-2 often finds itself stuck between a rock and a hard place; the rock in this analogy being [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and the hard place being [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]. Seriously, it's a Greek tragedy, the hand this little guy was dealt, as these two powerhouses have 885-2 almost entirely outclassed outside of a few niche situations. Comparing their stats at Lv.30, Ramen and Shigong's base HP range from ~16k-~20k depending on their [[Talents]], which at first glance, this cat's 58,650 base HP surpasses well over twofold. However, its knockback count cuts its endurance by two, meaning it only tanks 29,375 damage before each reposition. This isn't much better endurance than either of the aforementioned meatshields, especially not for 1,650¢. Its damage is also noticeably worse than both Ramen and Shigong's, and the 18-second recharge rate just adds insult to injury. It does have [[Wave Immunity]] going for it, giving it genuine leverage against [[Youcan]] if the circumstances call for it.

Realistically, its best use case is within mixed Angel/Zombie stages like [[Microscope Bridge]], where its range advantage allows it to function as a secondary layer of protection behind your main line. Even here, it doesn't particularly justify its price tag, since you can achieve much more by using said cash on another attacker. Its absence likely won't be felt either way; there are surely superior methods to harden your defenses without repeatedly taking out a loan all for this dollar store "tank". Furthermore, it only loses relevance as your Ramen and Shigong Cats gain even higher potential stats through +levels, eventually leaving 885-2 in their dust. It's good for early-midgame [[Zombie Outbreaks]] stages—before unlocking Shigong Cat—but that's as far as it goes.

